# CODEOWNERS — Phase 0 mobilisation (P0-03).
#
# Every handle below is a placeholder team, not a real GitHub team or user —
# this account has one collaborator (archivalg) today, so there is no real
# ownership split to encode yet. GitHub silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries
# that don't resolve to a real user/team with repo access, so until these
# placeholders are replaced with real handles (and those teams are actually
# granted write access to this repo), this file documents the intended
# routing but does not yet enforce required-reviewer routing on its own —
# that enforcement also needs P0-02's branch protection rules (rejected
# pull requests without CODEOWNERS approval), which is a repo-settings
# change no tool available in this session can make; see docs/adr/ for the
# decisions that gate real ownership assignment.
#
# Order matters: later patterns override earlier ones for a given path,
# same as .gitignore.

# Default: technical lead reviews anything not matched below.
*                                       @tempo-tech-lead

# Backend / optimisation API
/services/tempo-api/                   @tempo-backend-owners

# Security-sensitive backend surface — identity, tenant scope, action
# tokens, permissions. Kept distinct from the general backend pattern so a
# security reviewer is always requested, not just a backend reviewer.
/services/tempo-api/app/dependencies.py        @tempo-security-owners @tempo-backend-owners
/services/tempo-api/app/schemas/tenancy.py     @tempo-security-owners @tempo-backend-owners
/services/tempo-api/app/core/access_scope.py   @tempo-security-owners @tempo-backend-owners
/services/tempo-api/app/core/action_tokens.py  @tempo-security-owners @tempo-backend-owners
/services/tempo-api/app/models/identity.py     @tempo-security-owners @tempo-backend-owners
/services/tempo-api/app/errors.py              @tempo-security-owners @tempo-backend-owners

# Database migrations (Alembic, once Phase 2 adds it) — a DBA/platform
# reviewer, not just whoever wrote the backend change.
/services/tempo-api/alembic/           @tempo-platform-owners @tempo-backend-owners
/services/tempo-api/migrations/        @tempo-platform-owners @tempo-backend-owners

# Integration / connector runtime (Phase 3) — credential handling, vendor
# adapters.
/services/tempo-api/app/maestro/       @tempo-integration-owners @tempo-backend-owners

# Console (frontend)
/services/tempo-console/               @tempo-frontend-owners

# Infrastructure, CI/CD, and anything that touches deployment (Phase 8)
/.github/                              @tempo-platform-owners
/services/tempo-api/Dockerfile         @tempo-platform-owners
/services/*/Dockerfile                 @tempo-platform-owners

# Architecture decisions and this specification's own tracking documents
/docs/adr/                             @tempo-tech-lead @tempo-security-owners
/docs/                                 @tempo-tech-lead
